Problem: the managed .gitignore block lists every managed file path. `.claude/.gitignore` is normally committed (`git add .claude` takes it), but its block changes with machine state: an upstream skill gains a file, a wildcard gains an item, `skilletor.local.json` adds items, `vars` make an item render empty, auto-detected targets differ. Result: a committed file shows as modified after SessionStart syncs, with no project change behind it.

Fix (spec §6.3, §6.4, §14.2, §14.3 as rewritten for this card):
- Skills keep their directory name. Every installed skill dir gets a `.gitignore` containing `*` (plus a one-line comment), as a regular managed file of the item (in the lock, removed with the item). A source-shipped `.gitignore` at the skill root is replaced. Written whenever `gitignore` is enabled, both scopes, both harness roots (`.claude/skills`, `.agents/skills`); removed when disabled.
- Agents and rules install as `.local.<name>.md` (Claude) / `.local.<name>.toml` (Codex agents); a nested rule prefixes its file name (`rules/lang/.local.perl.md`). The prefix is part of the layout, independent of `gitignore`. Lock keys stay (`agents/foo`); only file paths change, so the first sync after the upgrade moves installed files by the normal diff (write new, delete old lock-owned path).
- Conflicts: an agent/rule item also claims its plain path; a foreign file at `agents/<name>.md` / `rules/<name>.md` is a conflict; `--force` removes it and installs the prefixed file.
- Blocks hold fixed entries only: `.claude` (project) = `skilletor.lock.json`, `skilletor.local.json`, `agents/**/.local.*`, `rules/**/.local.*`; `~/.claude` (in a work tree) = lock, state dir, same two patterns; `.codex` / `$CODEX_HOME` = `agents/**/.local.*`, `skilletor-rules.md`, only while that root holds managed Codex agents or the rules file; `.agents` = no block (an old per-path block there is removed).
- Commit hint: when sync creates a block or changes its content, the report says `<root>/.gitignore updated — commit it`.

Measured (2026-09-26): Claude Code 2.1.283 names a skill after its directory even with a frontmatter `name` (`.local.x/` → `/.local.x`), loads `agents/.local.x.md` and `rules/.local.x.md` (agent name from frontmatter; an agent without `name:` never loads, prefix or not); a skill dir with its own `*` .gitignore loads normally. Codex 0.153.4 skips a dot-prefixed skill dir, loads `.codex/agents/.local.x.toml`, loads a skill dir with its own .gitignore. `git status` check: the fixed patterns leave only own files, `skilletor.json` and the `.gitignore` visible.

